-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I17: TWO interfaces declare the same bare method name at
-- DIFFERENT dispatch argument indices, and NEITHER is nameable here -- this module imports
-- both of their modules but binds only `af` and `zf`.  So `mth` is not a shadow, the
-- occurrence is the standalone this module explicitly imported, and the answer is
-- 99 + 0 + 0 = 99.
--
-- This is #1351's graph, moved here when its must-fail pin drained.  Its `order-swapped`
-- twin ships beside it and is graded as its own row: the two differ ONLY in the order of
-- two import lines, and BEFORE the #1354-unit-A fix they disagreed about whether the
-- program even compiles -- this file printed 7 (the body of `impl IZ String`, reached
-- through IA's argument geometry) at exit 0, while the swapped file was REJECTED
-- `Type mismatch: Int vs String`.
--
-- HOW THE EXPECTED VALUE WAS ESTABLISHED -- derived, not captured.  #1351's own filing
-- hand-derived it before any fix existed: the call is `mth "abc" 5`, a String in FIRST
-- position, while `impl IZ String`'s method takes an Int first -- so reaching that body is
-- wrong under every reading, and the only defensible answers were the imported standalone
-- (99) or a rejection.  S1 then picks between them: neither interface is nameable here, so
-- `mth` is not a shadow and the standalone answers.
--
-- ⚠️ WHAT THIS DOES NOT ASSERT.  `universeMethodDispatchIdxRef` is still a bare
-- method-name-keyed list read first-match; this graph no longer REACHES it, because
-- shadow-hood is decided before the dispatch index is ever consulted.  The table's keying
